In PHP, closures (anonymous functions) do NOT automatically have access to variables from the outer scope. To access an outer variable, you must explicitly use the `use` keyword. Without `use`, the closure has its own scope and cannot see the outer variables.

For example:
```php
$x = 10;
$fn = function() {
    echo $x; // This will be null/undefined, not 10
};
```

So the statement "An anonymous function without `use` sees variables from the outer scope" is FALSE (неверно).

